 "caveats": [
  "Human baselines are not one thing: a single annotator on a subset (ImageNet), crowdworker majority votes (SQuAD, GLUE, SuperGLUE, HellaSwag), an estimate with no method (MNIST), an estimated expert level not measured on a panel (MMLU 89.8), selection-skewed validators (GPQA 81.3) or a lab's own recruited experts (GPQA 69.7), and tiny samples (MATH 90% = 18 of 20 problems). \"Passed human\" means passed that number.",
  "Leaderboards (SQuAD, GLUE, SuperGLUE) show one row per team, usually its best or latest submission; superseded earlier entries are invisible, so a per-year best can miss a submission that was later replaced.",
  "Mixed sources in the LLM era: paper and lab-reported numbers use their own prompting (CoT@32, cons@64, few-shot), Epoch runs use one harness. source_kind says which; a lab-reported first crossing is often a release event.",
  "Contamination: MMLU, HellaSwag, GSM8K, MATH, BBH and GPQA are public and appear in or near web training data; MMLU has about 6.5% erroneous questions (arXiv 2406.04127); GSM1k shows up to 8-point drops for some families (arXiv 2405.00332). ARC-AGI semi-private and private sets are held out but reused across many submissions.",
  "Dates: model release or paper v1 date. date_precision \"year\" uses July 1 of that year and \"month\" the 1st of the month, as chart placeholders; \"approx\" means the source date is ambiguous.",
  "Points marked verified \"(v)\" were taken from secondary tables or memory by the research pass and could not be confirmed from a primary page."
 ],
